---
import Base from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Section from '../components/Section.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL || '/';
---
<Base title="Privacy Policy — Compliance365" description="Our Privacy Policy aligns with the Australian Privacy Act 1988 (Cth) and the Australian Privacy Principles (APPs).">
  <Header />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="card">
        <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

        <!-- Plain language summary banner -->
        <div class="summary-banner">
          <p>
            <strong>We respect your privacy.</strong> We only collect what’s necessary to respond to your enquiries and deliver our services.
            We work securely within your environment and <strong>do not store or process any sensitive, confidential, or health-related data</strong> belonging to your organisation.
          </p>
        </div>

        <p>
          Compliance365 Pty Ltd (“Compliance365”, “we”, “us”, “our”) is committed to protecting your privacy in accordance with the
          <strong>Privacy Act 1988 (Cth)</strong> and the <strong>Australian Privacy Principles (APPs)</strong>.
        </p>

        <h2>1. Open and Transparent Management of Personal Information</h2>
        <p>
          This policy explains how we manage personal information. It is available on our website or by request via
          <a href="mailto:info@compliance365.com.au">info@compliance365.com.au</a>.
        </p>

        <h2>2. Anonymity and Pseudonymity</h2>
        <p>
          Wherever lawful and practical, you may choose to interact with us anonymously or under a pseudonym (e.g., when submitting general website enquiries).
        </p>

        <h2>3. Types of Personal Information We Collect</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Contact details (name, email address, organisation, phone number);</li>
          <li>Information provided through enquiry, contact, or download forms;</li>
          <li>Website usage data (e.g., cookies, IP address, pages visited, analytics via Google Analytics).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>4. How We Collect Personal Information</h2>
        <p>
          We collect personal information directly from you when you complete an online form, email us, or engage our services.
          We may also collect usage data through website analytics tools (e.g. Google Analytics).
        </p>

        <h2>5. Unsolicited Personal Information</h2>
        <p>
          If we receive personal information we did not request, we assess whether it could have been lawfully collected.
          If not, we delete or de-identify it as soon as practicable.
        </p>

        <h2>6. Purpose of Collection and Use</h2>
        <p>
          We collect and use personal information to:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Respond to your enquiries and provide requested information;</li>
          <li>Deliver and manage our compliance and assurance services;</li>
          <li>Improve our website and communications;</li>
          <li>Send updates, resources, or event invitations (with your consent).</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>7. Consent</h2>
        <p>
          By submitting personal information to us (e.g., via contact forms, email, or engagement), you consent to its collection, use, and disclosure in accordance with this Privacy Policy.
          You may withdraw consent at any time by contacting us at <a href="mailto:info@compliance365.com.au">info@compliance365.com.au</a>.
          Withdrawing consent may limit our ability to provide certain services or respond to enquiries.
        </p>

        <h2>8. Work Performed Within Client Environments</h2>
        <p>
          We deliver consulting and managed compliance services within our clients’ own secure environments (e.g., Microsoft 365, AWS, internal systems).
          We <strong>do not host, process, or store any sensitive, confidential, or health-related data</strong> belonging to client organisations.
          Access to client data is strictly limited to authorised personnel and used only for performing contracted services.
        </p>

        <h2>9. Disclosure of Personal Information</h2>
        <p>
          We may disclose limited personal information to trusted third-party providers who assist in operating our website and communications, such as:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Cloud/IT providers (Microsoft, AWS);</li>
          <li>Email/marketing platforms (e.g., HubSpot);</li>
          <li>Auditors, professional advisers, or regulators where legally required.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          Where data is stored overseas, we ensure appropriate safeguards are in place consistent with the APPs.
        </p>

        <h2>10. Direct Marketing</h2>
        <p>
          We may occasionally send marketing communications about our services or events (with your consent).
          You can opt out at any time by selecting “unsubscribe” or contacting us directly.
        </p>

        <h2>11. Cross-Border Disclosure</h2>
        <p>
          Some service providers (e.g., Microsoft 365, AWS, HubSpot) may store data outside Australia.
          These providers comply with recognised international privacy and security standards.
        </p>

        <h2>12. Government Identifiers</h2>
        <p>
          We do not use government-issued identifiers (such as TFNs, Medicare or driver licence numbers) as our own identifiers for individuals.
        </p>

        <h2>13. Quality of Personal Information</h2>
        <p>
          We take reasonable steps to ensure personal information we hold is accurate, complete, and up to date.
          You may request correction at any time.
        </p>

        <h2>14. Security and Retention</h2>
        <p>
          Personal information is stored securely with encryption, access controls, and audit logging.
          Data is retained only for as long as necessary for business or legal purposes, then securely deleted or de-identified.
        </p>

        <h2>15. Access and Correction</h2>
        <p>
          You may request access to, or correction of, your personal information by emailing
          <a href="mailto:info@compliance365.com.au">info@compliance365.com.au</a>.
          We will respond within a reasonable timeframe and may require verification of identity before providing access.
        </p>

        <h2>16. Cookies and Analytics</h2>
        <p>
          Our website uses cookies and analytics to monitor performance and improve usability.
          You may disable cookies via your browser settings, although some functionality may be limited.
        </p>

        <h2>17. Data Breach Notification</h2>
        <p>
          In the unlikely event of a data breach likely to cause serious harm, we will comply with the
          <strong>Notifiable Data Breaches (NDB) scheme</strong> and promptly notify affected individuals and the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC).
        </p>

        <h2>18. Contact Us</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy enquiries or complaints, please contact:
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Compliance365 Pty Ltd</strong><br>
          Email: <a href="mailto:info@compliance365.com.au">info@compliance365.com.au</a><br>
          Website: <a href="https://www.compliance365.com.au">www.compliance365.com.au</a>
        </p>
        <p class="muted small">Last updated: February 2026</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </Section>

  <Footer />
</Base>
